-names></name><name><surname>Yang</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Tarr</surname><given-names>PT</given-names></name><name><surname>Wu</surname><given-names>PH</given-names></name><name><surname>Handschin</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2005</year><article-title>Hyperlipidemic effects of dietary saturated fats mediated through PGC-1beta coactivation of SREBP.</article-title><source>Cell</source><volume>120</volume><fpage>261</fpage><lpage>273</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15680331</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="pone.0006066-Mao1"><label>8</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Mao</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>DeMayo</surname><given-names>FJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Li</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>bu-Elheiga</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Gu</surname><given-names>Z</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2006</year><article-title>Liver-specific deletion of acetyl-CoA carboxylase 1 reduces hepatic triglyceride accumulation without affecting glucose homeostasis.</article-title><source>Proc Natl Acad Sci U S A</source><volume>103</volume><fpage>8552</fpage><lpage>8557</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16717184</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="pone.0006066-Savage1"><label>9</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Savage</surname><given-names>DB</given-names></name><name><surname>Choi</surname><given-names>CS</given-names></name><name><surname>Samuel</surname><given-names>VT</given-names></name><name><surname>Liu</surname><given-names>ZX</given-names></name><name><surname>Zhang</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2006</year><article-title>Reversal of diet-induced hepatic steatosis and hepatic insulin resistance by ant